Wait for the PPC timer's measurement before the core is unloaded

CemuCommonInit's PPCTimer_init measures the TSC on a detached thread for
three seconds. When content fails sooner, in the first retro_run, the
frontend unloads the core while that thread still sleeps, and it then
wakes up in code that is no longer mapped. retro_deinit now waits for
the measurement once CemuCommonInit has run.

Upstream: https://github.com/WizzardSK/cemu-libretro/pull/37

--- a/src/libretro/CemuLibretro.cpp	2026-11-10 18:13:10.457565619 +0000
+++ b/src/libretro/CemuLibretro.cpp	2026-11-10 18:13:10.468066388 +0000
@@ -24,6 +24,7 @@
 
 #include "Cafe/CafeSystem.h"
 #include "Cafe/IOSU/legacy/iosu_act.h"
+#include "Cafe/HW/Espresso/PPCState.h"
 #include "Cafe/HW/Espresso/Recompiler/PPCRecompiler.h"
 #include "Cafe/OS/libs/coreinit/coreinit_Thread.h"
 #include "Cafe/OS/common/OSCommon.h"
@@ -6732,6 +6733,11 @@
 	// lock, which the thread needs in order to exit: the frontend hangs.
 	FileCache_StopAsyncWriter();
 
+	// CemuCommonInit's PPCTimer_init measures the TSC on a detached thread for
+	// three seconds, so a load that fails sooner would unload the library under it
+	if (s_cafe_system_initialized)
+		PPCTimer_waitForInit();
+
